# Security headers for Netlify / Cloudflare Pages.
# (Vite copies everything in /public to the site root, so this ships as-is.)
# For Vercel, the equivalent lives in vercel.json — KEEP THE TWO IN SYNC.
#
# CSP notes, so nothing gets loosened again by reflex:
#
#   script-src is 'self' only. It previously carried 'wasm-unsafe-eval' and
#   blob:, both of which existed solely for the Draco decoder in the old 3D
#   visualizer. That is gone, and blob: in script-src is a genuine XSS
#   amplifier — it lets injected code run a payload it assembles at runtime as
#   a Blob. Do not re-add either without a decoder that actually needs them.
#
#   blob: remains in img-src ONLY. The "upload your own tile" flow mints a
#   blob: URL and assigns it to an <img> (see visualizer2d/loadImage.js), which
#   is an img-src fetch. It is never fetched via XHR and never executed, so
#   connect-src / worker-src / child-src do not need it.
#
#   style-src keeps 'unsafe-inline' because React inline styles and Tailwind's
#   runtime classes require it. This is the one remaining relaxation.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; frame-src https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; child-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

# Long-cache the fingerprinted build assets.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
